      <div class="section-kicker"><span>03</span> Practical guides</div>
      <h1>Use the record. <em>Test the claim.</em></h1>
      <p class="content-lede">These resources help a technical, procurement, or operational lead turn a public claim about an agent system into a smaller set of evidence questions. They are not rankings, vendor recommendations, certifications, audits, or compliance advice.</p>
      <section class="content-block"><h2>Start with the decision in front of you</h2><p>The Field Index helps readers inspect standards, projects, and stewardship contexts. These supporting resources do something narrower: they help you ask what a proposed agent can do, what evidence supports that assertion, what remains unknown, and who owns the next answer.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/field-index">Browse the documented records <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p></section>
      <section class="content-block" aria-labelledby="resource-title"><h2 id="resource-title">Available resources</h2><div class="content-table-wrap"><table class="content-table"><thead><tr><th>Resource</th><th>When it helps</th><th>What it does not establish</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="/field-index/evaluate-agent-systems">Evaluate an agent system</a></td><td>You need a repeatable evidence frame before a pilot, procurement conversation, or integration decision.</td><td>That a vendor, standard, project, or deployment is safe, compliant, suitable, or endorsed.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/field-index/evidence-review-worksheet">Evidence review worksheet</a></td><td>You need one printable working record for evidence links, owners, limits, and decisions.</td><td>A security assessment, legal review, certification, or automated go/no-go decision.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
      <section class="content-block"><h2>How these guides are made</h2><p>The framework pages identify outside sources separately from Coreweaver’s own proposed method. Material claims include links and limits. If a source does not support a statement, the statement should be narrowed or removed rather than upgraded with confident language.</p><a class="text-link" href="/field-index/methodology">Read the Field Index methodology <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
